cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ClonoLoom in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ClonoLoom"
abstract: "A local-first workbench for adaptive immune receptor repertoires (T- and B-cell receptor sequencing, bulk and single-cell): validated reading of AIRR-C, Cell Ranger and immunoSEQ data, quality control, explicit clonotype definitions, diversity and overlap with their uncertainty, clonal tracking with expansion tests, specificity analysis, B-cell clonal families, germline reconstruction, somatic hypermutation, parsimony lineages and observed isotypes, single-cell expression maps, clonotype phenotypes, graph-based receptor/expression comparisons AnnData export, subject-level cohort comparisons, replicated count models, definition robustness, exploratory sequence signatures, contamination and batch evidence, and paired pseudobulk differential expression, with every step recorded. It runs locally as one self-contained program, needs no other software, and keeps the user's data on their computer."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: McDermott
    given-names: Robert
repository-code: "https://github.com/robert-mcdermott/clonoloom"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.8.0
keywords:
  - immune repertoire
  - AIRR-seq
  - T-cell receptor
  - B-cell receptor
  - clonotype
  - immunology
